    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d288">

                <pb facs="0397" n="329" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg329"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.711/1699½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">27 December, 1916</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have just been going
                    over the papers I brought down with me from Shadow Lawn, and come across
                        these.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d288-f1"/> I fear I have kept them too long. I
                    will be glad to discuss this and other kindred matters with you when we have
                    seen just what the several belligerents are willing to do about discussing terms
                    of peace.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d288-f1" n="18" xml:id="d288-f1-content">
                <p>Papers regarding interference with the mails.</p>
